  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 145 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nSunday we will start to see a shift in the upper level pattern as\na deep trough digs down the west coast. This will eventually turn\nthe upper winds to southwesterly next week. The small height falls\nassociated with this shift will allow for isolated convection each\nafternoon Monday through Wednesday. The most likely area for\nshowers will be the Coastal Plains where the moisture will be\ndeepest. Temperatures over the first half of the week will\nincrease a little each day. The low will see a more significant\nincrease with more overnight cloudiness especially over the I-35\nCorridor and Coastal Plains. The upper trough will move into the\ncentral Rockies by mid-week and bring a cold front into TX. The\nfront will move into the central/south Texas region by Thursday\nand through our CWA Friday. The front will bring chances for\nshowers and thunderstorms Thursday and Friday with the best\nchances early Friday. Models are showing some chance for locally\nheavy rain. We will have to see how this situation progresses\nthrough the coming days.",
